      \field{abstract}{Since the advent of the internet and the appearance of on-line music services, music listening and exchange habits have deeply evolved. Public libraries, which collections were until then mainly centered on CD, have been brought to think over their presence on music area, so as to stay in adequacy with the public's practices and needs. How can music sections keep fulflling their missions of development and dissemination of musical culture ? This dissertation aims at exploring the development of hybrid music collections and the enhancement of music among public libraries' music sections in the internet age, throughout the analysis of a set of initiatives and experiments.}
